    {
      "sourceParts": [
        {
          "sourceAlias": "L0130:S0",
          "verbatimText": "HTTP semantics ([HTTP]) are used for a broad range ofservices on the Internet. These semantics"
        },
        {
          "sourceAlias": "L0131:S0",
          "verbatimText": "have most commonly been used with HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2. HTTP/1.1 has been used over a variety"
        },
        {
          "sourceAlias": "L0132:S0",
          "verbatimText": "oftransport and session layers, while HTTP/2 has been used primarily with TLS over TCP. HTTP/3"
        },
        {
          "sourceAlias": "L0133:S0",
          "verbatimText": "supports the same semantics over a new transport protocol: QUIC."
        }
